cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LiNaK: an alkali-atom AMO pipeline"
message: "If you use LiNaK, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Antoury
    given-names: Youssef
    email: Joeantouri98@gmail.com
keywords:
  - AMO
  - alkali atoms
  - Rydberg
  - polarizability
  - Feshbach
  - optical tweezers
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-06"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  LiNaK is a Python NIST/QDT toolkit for neutral alkali atoms (Li–Fr):
  levels, transitions, lifetimes, polarizability, BBR, tweezers, hyperfine,
  and Feshbach, with optional ORCA (Neese) and ARC bridges. Limited support
  for ions and 3d metals (Fe, Cr).
url: "https://github.com/joeantouri98-sketch/LiNaK"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joeantouri98-sketch/LiNaK"
